Acknowledgments=20


As co-founders of the 9/11 Consensus Panel, we would first like to=20
extend our great thanks to the 23 expert reviewers who accepted=20
our invitation to join an exacting review project in 2011, most of=20
whom have served it each year until the present.=20

They are: Dr. Robert Bowman (1934-2013) (former Director=20
of Advanced Space Programs Development, [=E2=80=9CStar Wars=E2=80=9D]);=20
David S. Chandler (physics and mathematics teacher); Giulietto=20
Chiesa (Italian journalist, former member, European Parliament);=20
Jonathan Cole (professional civil engineer); Dwain Deets (former=20
aerospace research director, NASA); Tod Fletcher (1952-2014)=20
(former geography and environmental science instructor at=20
Berkeley); Dr. Daniele Ganser (Swiss historian); Lt. Col. David=20
Gapp (US Air Force retired pilot and aircraft accident investiga-=20
tor); Dr. Niels Harrit (Associate Professor Emeritus of Chemistry,=20
Copenhagen); Dr. Steven E. Jones (Professor Emeritus of Physics,=20
Brigham Young University); Commander Ralph Kolstad (retired=20
US Navy fighter pilot, airline pilot); Dr. Graeme MacQueen,=20
Professor Emeritus Peace Studies, McMaster University, Canada);=20
Massimo Mazzucco (award-winning filmmaker, screenwriter,=20
journalist); P. Dennis McMahon (attorney for 9/11 families); Aidan=20
Monaghan (B.S. in electronic engineering); Rowland Morgan=20
(former journalist, The Guardian and The Independent); Frances=20
Shure (Licensed Professional Counselor); Lou Stolzenberg (retired=20
physical therapist); Daniel Sunjata (American actor in film, televi-=20
sion and theater); Tony Szamboti (B.S. Mechanical Engineering);=20
William Veale (attorney, retired instructor at UC Berkeley School=20
of Law); Dr. Matthew Witt (Professor of Public Administration,=20
University of La Verne, CA); Dr. Jonathan B. Weisbuch, M.D. (for-=20
mer senior public health officer in Arizona and Wyoming).=20

We further wish to thank the seven Honorary Members who=20
lent their considerable weight to supporting this project: James=20
